verdicts.reason:
The core attributed fact holds. TNM, 24 Sep 2019: 'The TDP has now in turn alleged that the YSRCP has shown unfair preference while awarding the contract, with TDP chief and former Chief Minister Chandrababu Naidu calling the process 'reserve tendering' and not reverse tendering.' The contract in question is the one TNM says was going to MEIL. Naidu is a named party, a contra exists (c007), and the edge is explicitly framed as unproven, so 'alleged' is the right tier. It is not killed.

Three fields are imprecise:
- **MEIL is not named in Naidu's words.** TNM says 'unfair preference while awarding the contract' and names MEIL elsewhere in the article. 'Favouring MEIL' is a fair inference, not a quote.
- **CAG's 'incorrect' refers to a narrower figure.** CAG says 'The claim of the government that 12.60 per cent less than ECV was incorrect', i.e. the Rs 628.43 cr Part A saving. It did not rule on the aggregate Rs 780 cr figure the claim sets next to it.
- **The closing clause undersells CAG.** 'Did not find for whom it was reserved' is literally true, since CAG makes no finding of intent or tailoring for MEIL. But CAG goes further than the text admits:
  - it titled the section 'Arbitrariness in selection of contract agency and undue benefit thereon';
  - it found that stringent conditions plus a shortened bid window 'restricted participation of other bidders', so the tender 'resulted in a single bidder, who could fulfill the modified conditions';
  - it recorded SEW Infrastructure's Sep 2019 complaint that the conditions 'suited only one or two firms in the entire country', which drew no action;
  - it quantified a Rs 233.26 cr 'undue advantage to the contractor' on add-on works.

  The government accepted the observation in Nov 2024, conceding 'due to selective modification of tender conditions only one bidder participated'. That concession came from Naidu's own administration, so it is not independent corroboration of his 2019 allegation. The upgradeIf condition (a finding that conditions were altered to exclude specific bidders) is partly approached but not met.
